  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Spot Hearts. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Hearts variant: spot cards have point values; face cards zero.',
    objective: 'The object is to avoid scoring penalty points. Each heart scores its pip value (2–10 at face value, jack 11, queen 12, king 13, ace 14; queen of spades 25). The game is played to a higher target (e.g. 500); the player with the lowest score when someone reaches or exceeds the target wins.',
    gameplay: 'Play follows standard Hearts. The holder of the 2 of clubs leads it to the first trick. Players must follow the suit led if possible; the highest card of the suit led wins the trick. Hearts may not be led until a heart has been played to a previous trick (hearts broken), unless a player holds only hearts. Shooting the moon (taking all penalty cards) reverses the score for that hand. Deal and passing cycle are as in standard Hearts.',
    keyRules: [
      'Spot scoring',
      'Pip-value hearts',
      'Queen of spades 25',
      'Follow suit',
      'No leading hearts until broken',
      'Shooting the moon reverses points',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'Four players. Spot Hearts is most commonly played by four; there are no formal partnerships.',
      deck: 'A standard 52-card deck is used, with no jokers. All 52 cards are dealt out one at a time so each player receives 13 cards. Spot Hearts uses the same deck as standard Hearts; only the penalty scoring differs (hearts count their pip value, queen of spades 25).',
      equipment: 'A standard 52-card deck is used, with no jokers. All 52 cards are dealt out one at a time so each player receives 13 cards. Spot Hearts uses the same deck as standard Hearts; only the penalty scoring differs (hearts count their pip value, queen of spades 25).',
      dealing: 'Deal and play are clockwise. All 52 cards are dealt out one at a time so that each player has 13. After the deal, each player passes three cards face-down (first hand to the left, second to the right, third across, fourth hand no pass; the cycle repeats).',
    },
    turnFlow: 'Play follows standard Hearts. The holder of the 2 of clubs leads it to the first trick. Players must follow the suit led if possible; the highest card of the suit led wins the trick. Hearts may not be led until a heart has been played to a previous trick (hearts broken), unless a player holds only hearts. Shooting the moon (taking all penalty cards) reverses the score for that hand. Deal and passing cycle are as in standard Hearts.',
